From dc313e0eee439a9f1ecbd286f43662e9601cd9ef Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jiaxing Hu <gahing@gahingwoo.com>
Date: Tue, 11 Aug 2026 16:30:39 +1200
Subject: [PATCH] rocket RK3576: do not write the scale table over the first
 conv's operand

fill_regcmd_firstconv points 0x5024, the second SDP operand, at
bias_addr + 0x100 and always has, while the generic path computes it. For 32
output channels rkt_coef_table_bytes() is 4 * 64 = 256, which is 0x100, so the
fp16 scale entries were being written exactly on top of the first conv's
operand.

Measured on conv0: the round 52 arrangement gives distinct 1 with all 32
channels constant and an output of exactly 128 plus the OUT_CVT offset, with
no accumulator contribution at all, while both knobs that skip the block,
ROCKET_FS_ZERO and ROCKET_FS_FLOATS, give distinct 254 with 4 constant
channels and give it identically. The operand value is inert there, 0x0e0e, 0
and 0x3fc4 all dead alike, so it is the write and not the content.

A first conv now leaves that region zero and does not get the single constant
word either. ROCKET_FC_SCALE_TABLE forces the table back on as a control.

This does not make conv0 correct; it un-regresses it to computing something
wrong rather than nothing, which is where it was before round 52.

Signed-off-by: Jiaxing Hu <gahing@gahingwoo.com>
---
 src/gallium/drivers/rocket/rkt_coefs.c | 37 ++++++++++++++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 35 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/gallium/drivers/rocket/rkt_coefs.c b/src/gallium/drivers/rocket/rkt_coefs.c
index 1a8861f..cdd2444 100644
--- a/src/gallium/drivers/rocket/rkt_coefs.c
+++ b/src/gallium/drivers/rocket/rkt_coefs.c
@@ -1036,7 +1036,40 @@ biases_done:
              *
              * ROCKET_SCALE_OFF restores the single word at groups*64.
              */
-            bool scale_table = getenv("ROCKET_SCALE_OFF") == NULL;
+            /*
+             * The FIRST CONV wants this region left ZERO.
+             *
+             * conv0 is 32 of 32 channels constant with the arrangement round
+             * 52 made the default, and its output is exactly 128 plus the
+             * OUT_CVT offset with no accumulator contribution at all: sweeping
+             * the output shift over 2^16 does not move a bit of it. Both knobs
+             * that skip this block entirely, ROCKET_FS_ZERO and
+             * ROCKET_FS_FLOATS, bring the MAC back and bring it back
+             * IDENTICALLY, distinct 254 with 4 constant channels, so the
+             * content of the region is irrelevant and only writing to it is
+             * not. ROCKET_SCALE_OFF, which still writes one word there, sits
+             * in between at distinct 60.
+             *
+             * The mechanism is an address collision. fill_regcmd_firstconv
+             * points 0x5024, the second SDP operand, at bias_addr + 0x100 and
+             * always has, while the generic path computes it. For 32 output
+             * channels rkt_coef_table_bytes() is 4 * 64 = 256, which IS 0x100,
+             * so round 52 began writing the fp16 scale entries exactly on top
+             * of the first conv's operand.
+             *
+             * Round 52 changed this for every operation and was regression
+             * tested only on the shapes that already passed. conv0 was not
+             * among them, so this went unseen; it is in the regression set
+             * permanently now.
+             *
+             * ROCKET_FC_SCALE_TABLE forces the table on for a first conv, as
+             * the control.
+             */
+            bool first_conv = rkt_screen(pcontext->screen)->soc == RKT_SOC_RK3576 &&
+                              !rkt_is_depthwise(poperation) &&
+                              poperation->input_tensors[0]->dims[3] <= 4;
+            bool scale_table = getenv("ROCKET_SCALE_OFF") == NULL &&
+                               (!first_conv || getenv("ROCKET_FC_SCALE_TABLE"));
             if (scale_table) {
                uint16_t *sc16 = (uint16_t *)(b8 + table_bytes);
                const float *wsc = poperation->conv.weight_tensor->scales;
@@ -1093,7 +1126,7 @@ biases_done:
             unsigned n = fill ? strtoul(fill, NULL, 0) : 1;
             if (n == 0 || n > cap)
                n = cap;
-            if (!scale_table)
+            if (!scale_table && !first_conv)
                for (unsigned i = 0; i < n; i++)
                   fs32[i] = 0x1004;
          } else if (getenv("ROCKET_FS_FLOATS") ||
-- 
